I am working on an alternate text-based interface for NetHack that
uses the high-level curses routines (the tty port sometimes links with
curses, but only uses the low-level terminal routines).  It is a
separate codebase from the tty code, and does not modify the existing
tty code in any way.  I am wanting to find out how much interest there
is in the community for this, both for users and those who might want
to help with the development effort.

Some of the advantages over the traditional TTY code include:

 * Configurable placement of status and message windows relative to
the map
 * Better handling of terminal windows larger and smaller than the
"standard" 80x24
 * Less platform dependencies (the curses library takes care of many
of these)
 * Can link with PDCurses for SDL to remove the terminal dependency
entirely (e.g. for a Mac OS Classic or a PDA port)
 * Eye-candy (window-borders, optional popup-dialogs, etc)

